<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shattiwaza</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shattiwaza was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni</a> in the fourteenth century BCE. After the assassination of his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tushratta">Tushratta</a> and a disputed succession, he turned to the Hittite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suppiluliuma-i">Suppiluliuma I</a>. Accounts of the Mitanni Empire note that Suppiluliuma installed him as a Hittite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>, ending Mitanni's independence.</p></div>
